# Automation Isolation — {{project_name}}

This file is the operator's per-capability registry of credential scope, data isolation, and spend governance for every enabled autonomous capability in {{project_name}}.

**When to complete this file:** fill in a capability entry the first time this project enables an autonomous capability (a scheduled run, a parallel build, a write-back capability) — before it first runs. Do not fill it in speculatively at INIT — a project with no enabled automation leaves this file empty, except for the high-blast-radius surface list below, which the operator declares before enabling the *first* capability.

For the doctrine each entry must satisfy, see: `core/methodology/least-privilege-isolation.md` (non-production default, least privilege, pinned config, defense-in-depth) and `core/methodology/spend-governance.md` (provider cap, soft ceiling, stop condition). This file and `core/governance/KILL-SWITCH.md` together answer "is this capability safe to enable": this one declares what it runs as, what it can reach, and what it costs; KILL-SWITCH declares how it is stopped.

