## Enabled-Capability Registry

*One entry per enabled autonomous capability. Add an entry when you enable the capability; mark it retired (with date) when you disable it.*

### Capability: [name]

*(Copy and complete this block for each enabled capability.)*

**Environment and data:** [What environment this capability runs against. Non-production by default; if production, state the explicit rationale. Name the data source and confirm it satisfies DATA-POLICY (synthetic / anonymized seeds for dev data).]

**Credential scope:** [The identity this capability runs as and the exact permissions it holds — what it can read, what it can write, and why nothing narrower suffices. Read-only unless a listed function requires write. Never merge or admin scope.]

**Cannot reach:** [What this credential demonstrably cannot touch — the declared high-blast-radius surfaces above, production data stores, secrets outside its scope. Stated so it can be verified, not assumed.]

**Config control:** [Where this capability's automation config lives, who reviews changes to it, and confirmation that its third-party dependencies are version-pinned to immutable references.]

**Spend cap (provider backstop):** [The provider-side hard ceiling set on this capability's credential before enablement. Amount and scope. "n/a" is not accepted — every capability with model API access must carry a cap.]

**Soft per-run ceiling:** [The live-tally token/cost limit at which a single run self-halts. State the limit and the unit (tokens, estimated cost). If the capability has no per-run ceiling — state "n/a" with rationale — note that the provider backstop above remains required.]

**Spend attribution:** [How this capability's spend is read: which distinct credential's provider usage view, and at what cadence the operator reviews it.]

**Stop condition:** [The measurable criterion at which this capability is halted and its value-to-cost ratio reviewed. Includes spend threshold, win criterion (what counts as a win), and kill criterion (what outcome at what spend level triggers disabling). Reads from existing records (verifier reviews, cockpit/flight-plan logs, pilot telemetry) — does not create new ones.]

